# Selection tiles: the tile is the check

When the user picks **one option out of a few**, and each option has a title (plus an optional
icon and a short description) — export type, print layout, download vs. email — render the
options as **selectable tiles**, not as radio buttons.

The tile **is** the control. Its own border and background show which one is selected; there is
no radio dot (or checkbox) inside it.

## Do

- Use `BillingOptionTile` (`components/billing/billing-action-dialog.tsx`), laid out in a grid:
  `grid gap-1.5 sm:grid-cols-N`.
- Selected: `border-primary/55 bg-primary/5 ring-1 ring-primary/25`. Unselected:
  `border-border/80 bg-card hover:bg-muted/40`. That change is the only selection indicator.
- The whole tile is one `<button type="button">` with `cursor-pointer`, `aria-pressed={selected}`
  and a visible focus ring, so keyboard and screen-reader users still get the state.
- If another module needs the same pattern, move the tile to `components/shared/` and reuse it.
  Never copy the markup.

## Do NOT

- Put a radio dot or a checkbox inside the tile. It repeats what the tile already shows and adds
  noise.
- Build the pattern as a `RadioGroup` with cards used as labels.

## When NOT to use tiles

- More than ~5 options, or options with no description → `Select` / `SearchableCombobox`.
- On/off or multi-select options → `BillingToggleRow` / checkboxes.

## Example

```tsx
// ✅ The tile is the selection
<div className="grid gap-1.5 sm:grid-cols-3">
  <BillingOptionTile
    selected={kind === 'invoice'}
    onSelect={() => setKind('invoice')}
    title={t('invoices.bulkExportTypeInvoice')}
    description={t('invoices.bulkExportTypeInvoiceHint')}
    icon={List}
  />
</div>

// ❌ Radio dot inside the tile
<button type="button" className="… rounded-lg border …">
  <span className="size-4 rounded-full border …" />
  …
</button>
```
